.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt RTWSDIO 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rtwsdio
.Nd Realtek RTL8723DS SDIO wireless driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "rtwsdio* at sdmmc?"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver matches function 1 of SDIO devices with vendor 0x024c
and product 0xd723.
It loads and validates RTL8723D firmware through
.Xr firmload 9 .
Without an explicit radio profile, the driver only bootstraps firmware.
It does not attach a network interface in that mode.
With a valid profile, it attaches a station interface for legacy 2.4 GHz
802.11b/g and WPA2.
The initial profile does not enable HT or WME.
Radio operation requires device and board validation.
.Pp
The native host must be enabled in the device tree,
marked non-removable and connected to a registered standard MMC power sequence.
Diagnostic SDIO profiles are excluded.
The board configuration owns power resources, polarity and delays.
The driver does not operate board GPIOs or regulators.
A disabled board profile remains disabled.
.Pp
Both the host and card must support a 512-byte block size.
The driver checks the card CIS and verifies block-size writes by readback.
It preserves other functions' enable bits.
A per-device executor serializes sleepable bus operations.
In bootstrap-only mode, operational receive and transmit interrupts remain
masked.
A failed or uncertain FIFO transfer blocks further CMD53 transfers.
Detach retains resources until the transport can be safely released.
.Sh RADIO PROFILE
A profile must be supplied as properties of the SDIO child device.
The driver does not inherit properties from its parent.
The
.Sq rtw88-regulatory
dictionary requires the
.Sq world-min
domain and a nonzero
.Sq channels-2ghz
bit mask for channels 1 through 13.
The
.Sq rtw8723d-phy-package
property supplies the package selector.
A platform
.Sq mac-address
may replace the address read from EFUSE.
An incomplete profile is rejected.
The board provider remains responsible for supplying a valid policy.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa /libdata/firmware/rtw88/rtw8723d_fw.bin
RTL8723D firmware, supplied by the Ports rtw88-firmware package.
Other configured
.Xr firmload 9
search roots are also supported.
.El
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It firmware ready (bootstrap only)
The chip reported completion of the firmware bootstrap.
This message does not establish radio or network readiness.
.It native attach unavailable: errno
The host does not satisfy admission or core attachment failed.
.It bootstrap or netif attach failed: errno
Firmware, transport, profile or network attachment failed.
.It attach cleanup retained ownership: errno
Cleanup could not confirm resource release.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sdmmc 4 ,
.Xr firmload 9
.Sh LIMITATIONS
Host contract tests and target compilation do not establish physical
power, SDIO interrupt delivery, firmware start or WLAN operation.
Board enablement and hardware acceptance require separate validation.
